# Every *page* is prerendered, so this `/*` block covers the static responses
# Cloudflare Pages serves. The one exception is POST /api/contact, which renders
# on demand: header rules apply to static assets, not to worker responses, so
# that route sets its own Content-Type and Cache-Control in code. It returns
# JSON or a redirect and never HTML, so nothing below is load-bearing for it.
# The full script/style CSP is generated per-page by Astro's native security.csp
# feature (astro.config.mjs) as a <meta> tag, because it must hash Astro's own
# inlined scripts/styles — those hashes can't live in a static header.
# The header CSP below is deliberately the *complementary* subset: only
# directives that (a) a <meta> tag can't express (frame-ancestors) or (b) don't
# govern scripts/styles (object-src, base-uri). It intentionally omits
# default-src/script-src/style-src — putting those here would become the
# fallback for the inline scripts and block Astro's hashed markup. So the two
# policies compose instead of colliding, and frame-ancestors now covers the one
# gap X-Frame-Options was carrying alone.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
